{"source": "function Unresolved_2e1a7d4d(uint256 arg0) public {
        require(uint8(uint256(store_f) / 0x010000000000000000000000000000000000000000) == 0, CustomError_9e87fac8());
        require(unresolved_70a08231[msg.sender] >= arg0, CustomError_f4d678b8());
        unresolved_70a08231[msg.sender] = unresolved_70a08231[msg.sender] - arg0;
        emit Event_ddf252ad(msg.sender, address(0), arg0);
    }", "notes": "The probe withdraws 1000 (0x3e8) after minting 1000 to the sender; reference ok=true and the follow-up balanceOf returns 0, so the withdraw must actually burn the sender's tokens. The candidate was `view` and only did the two requires, never decrementing unresolved_70a08231, so its balanceOf still returned 0x3e8. Kept the paused flag check (byte 2 of store_f, matching Unresolved_8456cb59/Unresolved_3f4ba83a pause toggling) and the sufficient-balance require with CustomError_f4d678b8, then added the balance decrement on unresolved_70a08231 and the standard Transfer event to satisfy step 0 ok and step 1 balance==0."}
